course: dictionary
lesson: 8254
title: One word, many ribbons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A ribbon is a long, narrow strip of cloth used for tying, decorating or wrapping. It can also be a prize, or any long, narrow strip at all. Read the words around it to find the meaning that fits.
explain: «Three fourths of a ribbon is 18 cm» is about cloth you can measure, so the ribbon is the strip of cloth. «Imagine a long green ribbon of fields on a huge sandy map» is about shape: the fields are long and narrow like a strip, so ribbon means any long, narrow strip.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it into the sentence in place of the word. If «a red ribbon» means a red strip of cloth, the sentence still makes sense. If you swap in «a red prize» and it still makes sense, the context may be about a prize too, so check the other clues.
fact: A ribbon is a long, narrow strip of cloth used for tying, decorating or wrapping.
fact: A ribbon can be a prize or badge, such as a blue ribbon for first place.
fact: A ribbon can be any long, narrow strip, such as «a ribbon of river wound through the valley».
fact: «Cut to ribbons» means cut into many pieces.
fact: Cutting a log or a ribbon into pieces always takes one cut fewer than the number of pieces: the last piece needs no cut.
exercise: «Her hair was tied up with a red ribbon.» What is a ribbon in this sentence? | A river that winds through a valley | A piece of paper for writing | *A long, narrow strip of cloth used for tying | A prize for coming first
exercise: «Her science project won a blue ribbon at the school fair.» What does ribbon mean here? | A rope for climbing | A long strip of road | *A prize or badge for first place | A strip of cloth for wrapping presents
exercise: «Leo's kite was cut to ribbons by the thorny bush.» What does «cut to ribbons» mean? | *Cut into many pieces | Tied in a bow | Wrapped carefully in paper | Measured with a ruler
test: «Three fourths of a ribbon is 18 cm.» How long is the whole ribbon? | 18 cm | 36 cm | 6 cm | *24 cm
test: A ribbon is cut into 4 pieces. How many cuts were needed? | *3 | 1 | 2 | 4
exam: «A ribbon 3 metres long is 300 centimetres; cutting off 45 centimetres leaves 255 centimetres.» After 45 centimetres is cut off a 3-metre ribbon, how long is the ribbon left? | 300 centimetres | 45 centimetres | *255 centimetres | 345 centimetres
